A||||41||JBGehling||Poll: Favorite Fiero model/year||||1||
Z||000000||JBGehling||01-20-2001||07:59 PM||||I know this has probably been beat into the ground, but I was wondering what everyone's favorite year/model is (based solely on looks, not performance)?<BR>  <BR>       I have to admit, even though I own two 88's (yellow formula and red GT), I still love the look of a good 86-87 GT. I just think they look a lot more stylish with the silver ground marks and MUCH nicer interior.<BR>       Coming in a very close second is the 86-87 SE's. I know, I know... the 85 GT is practically the same car, but I think the black ground marks look better than the grey on the notchback.<P>       I'm not a big fan of many other fieros, but here's my list:<P>1.86-87 GT<BR>2.88 GT<BR>3.86-87 SE<BR>4.85 GT<BR>5.84 Indy<BR>6.84 coupe<BR>7.88 formula (I sorta inherited mine...)<P><BR>There you have my opinion, how about yours?<BR>Josh<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||01-20-2001||08:08 PM||||1.) 87/88 Coupes...88 Formulas<BR>2.) 88 GTs (I like the monochrome look much better than the silver/black aero pieces)<BR>I actually really like the looks of the 84-86 coupes as well, the original.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||01-20-2001||08:18 PM||||1. 88 GT's<BR>2. 85 GT's<BR>3. Any other fiero<P>I love the monochrome look of the 88's also. I also like the 85 GTs for some reason, maybe because they are the only notchback GT made.||||reg||1
Z||000003||JBGehling||01-20-2001||08:23 PM||||I know what you mean about the 85 GT's, I'm not generally a notchback Fiero fan, but there's something about the 85 GT's notchback that puts it above the coupe's and the formula... ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cooter||01-20-2001||08:32 PM||||1- 88 GT<BR>2- The 84 Pace Car, the one that started it all  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||01-20-2001||09:05 PM||||For me, it really depends on body color.<P>Generally, though, my list goes:<BR>STDII<BR>Aero-notchback<BR>STDI<BR>All Fastbacks<P>STDI is my first choice if it's red<BR>Aero-notchback is my first choice if it's black<BR>STDII is my first choice almost no matter what color<BR>Fastback, I don't really have any preference, but the mono paint schemes do look better than the two tone.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 01-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fformula88||01-20-2001||10:36 PM||||I'll give one guess...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I love the 87-88 notchbacks!  I think the GT's are very good looking also.  I actually like the GT's the best, but the notchbacks are right up there. <P>I also really like the Indy's.  The white with silver bottom and the red stripe really make it sharp!  Someday maybe I can pick one up.<P>------------------<BR>John<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/formula2m6/FIEROSIG1.JPG">    <BR>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1997 Ford Probe SE<BR>AOL IM: Fformula88||||reg||1
